        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The 505 CST is worth its reputation for one specific reason: a
            <strong class="text-white">published 325 lb capacity</strong> at a price where 300 is
            the ceiling, backed by a ten-year frame warranty. Capacity is the best available proxy
            for frame rigidity, and rigidity is what separates a budget machine you enjoy from one
            you tolerate.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy it as hardware, not as a platform — it runs manually, which is what matters. Then
            read <a href="/treadmill-maintenance/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">the maintenance schedule</a>,
